$bog_vmap_app_palette $mol_view
	- Links separated by commas. The first http(s) one is the donor pack, the rest
	- are lands of Giper Baza holding component sources; anything else is refused
	- and said so under the field. Stored exactly as typed, see `pack_link`.
	links? \https://mol.hyoo.ru
	query? \
	selected? \
	- Narrow layout for a side panel of the editor: header in a column, ports pane
	- dropped. A port row is an 11rem signature plus a value plus an owner badge and
	- does not fit a panel; the ports of a node picked on the canvas belong to the
	- inspector of 2.6 anyway, which is a different question from «what can I add».
	compact false
	- Class the pointer is currently carrying, empty when nothing is being dragged,
	- and where the pointer is right now in viewport coordinates. Started here on
	- `pointerdown`, moved and cleared by whoever owns the canvas: the palette knows
	- when a drag begins and nothing about where it ends.
	dragged? \
	drag_x? 0
	drag_y? 0
	- Classes of the attached lands, handed in by the owner. The palette knows no
	- database: whoever does resolves the links of the field and passes the trees,
	- and the library resolves them against the pack like any other class.
	land_classes /$mol_tree2
	attr *
		^
		bog_vmap_app_palette_compact <= compact
	sub <= body /$mol_view
	-
	Head $mol_bar
		sub /
			<= Brand $mol_view sub / \Палитра
			<= Links $mol_string
				hint \Пак и ленды через запятую
				value? <=> links?
			<= Query $mol_string
				hint \Поиск по имени
				value? <=> query?
			<= Total $mol_view sub / <= total \
	-
	- What was typed and not taken, and why, right under the field. Rendered only
	- while there is something to say: a second pack is refused by construction
	- and a person who typed one has to learn that from the screen, not from a log.
	Note $mol_view
		sub / <= rejected_note \
	-
	Body $mol_view
		sub <= body_content /$mol_view
	-
	Classes $mol_scroll
		sub /
			<= Class_list $mol_list
				rows <= class_rows /
	-
	- `$mol_scroll` is a grid that puts every child into cell 1/1, so it holds
	- exactly one node. The heading has to live beside it, not in it.
	Ports $mol_view
		sub /
			<= Ports_head $mol_view
				sub /
					<= Selected $mol_view sub / <= selected_title \
					<= Chain $mol_view sub / <= chain_title \
			<= Ports_scroll $mol_scroll
				sub /
					<= Port_list $mol_list
						rows <= port_rows /
	-
	- One button per class. `$mol_list` renders only what is on screen, so all
	- 449 of them cost nothing until scrolled to.
	Class_row* $bog_vmap_app_palette_item
		title <= class_title* \
		click? <=> class_click*? null
		current <= class_current* false
		drag_start? <=> class_drag*? null
	-
	Port_row* $bog_vmap_app_palette_port
		sign <= port_sign* \
		body <= port_body* \
		owner <= port_owner* \
		inherited <= port_inherited* false
	-
	- The model. The pack address is DERIVED from the field: the first http(s) link
	- of the list, with its slash grown here and not in the field, so that typing
	- an address is possible at all. Empty when the list names no pack, and the
	- library is then the lands alone.
	Lib $bog_vmap_lib
		pack <= pack_link \
		classes <= land_classes
